hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"405","Ahmad ibn 'Abdah narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Abu Harun al-Madani, he said: In the house of al-'Abbas there was a spout pouring into the mosque, then 'Umar came and removed it. Al-'Abbas said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) himself placed it with his hand. 'Umar said: ""You shall have no ladder except my back until you restore it to its place."" Abu Dawud said: This is the brother of 'Isa the grocer, Abu Harun, while 'Isa is the tailor — the grocer and the clothes-beater — and he is 'Isa ibn Maysarah, and his brother is unobjectionable."
"406","Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Qattan narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman — meaning Ibn Maghra' — narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from his uncle Wasi' ibn Habban, he said: Abu Lubabah had a date-cluster in the garden of a man, so he spoke to him saying: You tread upon my garden to reach your cluster; I shall give you one like it in your garden, so remove it from me. He refused him, so he spoke to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about it. He said: ""O Abu Lubabah, take a cluster like yours, join it to your property, and withhold from your companion what he dislikes."" He said: I will not do it. He said: ""Then go and cut for him a cluster like his into his garden, then build a wall above that, for there is no harm nor reciprocal harm in Islam."" Abu Dawud said: Al-'adhq with a fathah is the palm tree, and al-'idhq with a kasrah is the cluster."
"407","'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, from 'Abdullah Ibn al-Mubarak — and I read it to Sa'id ibn Ya'qub from Ibn Mubarak — from Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not cause harm to one another in digging."" Sa'id added: That is when a man digs beside another man to take away his water."
